# Batch files are written to the working folder with Windows line endings, whatever
# core.autocrlf says. In one with Unix endings cmd.exe looks for a label 512 bytes at a
# time and loses one that the edge of a read cuts in two.
#
# What git stores does not change: Unix endings, as upstream has them, so a merge sees
# nothing of this. Do not widen the rule to other files, a dozen of which are stored
# with Windows endings and one with both. CLAUDE.md has the rest.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
